
╭────────╮╭───────────────────╮                                                 
│  tray╭────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮       
│      │                                                                │───────
│      │       tray is a task manager in two layers. Dump any task,     │      │
│     t│       or a half-thought, into the garage for the month you     │      │
│  ▸  R│       expect to pick it up. Take it onto the tray when ready.  │      │
│     C│       ╭─ garage ────────────╮       ╭─ tray ──────────────╮    │      │
│     B│       │ anything, any month │  ────▶│ what you do now     │    │      │
│     R│       │ no structure asked  │  ◀────│ priority, due, tags │    │      │
│      │       ╰─────────────────────╯       ╰─────────────────────╯    │      │
│      │       (a)dd    a line to the layer you are on                  │      │
│      │       (t)ake   a garage line onto the tray, structured         │      │
│      │       (d)      hand a tray task back to the garage             │      │
│      │       (enter)  act on the selection; the menu lists the rest   │      │
│      │       ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │      │
│      │       keys                  acting                             │      │
│      │       ↑↓  j k move          a       add     d       hand back  │      │
│      │       tab     switch layer  t       take    >       move to    │      │
│      │       space   select        r       retake  D       delete     │      │
│      │       /       filter        x       done    R       restore    │      │
│      │       v       show done                                        │      │
│      │                                                                │      │
└──────╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯──────┘
